    "divergence_from_contract_call_1": {
      "contract_states": "16 exact_named_gene + 6 via_composite_label = 22 unique genes",
      "phase7_recomputes": "16 exact_named_gene + 7 composite-only = 23 unique genes",
      "extra_gene": "CEMIP",
      "cause": "Contract Call 1 enumerated only the family/pathway/complex labels (56 of the 212 in-stratum Phase 1b rows). CEMIP is reached through `HYALURONAN`, whose label_type is `other`, so Call 1's enumeration did not cover it. Phase 7 expands every Phase 1b row that carries constituent_genes, which is the rule phase3b_coverage.py used and is why the 27 gene-per-stratum total reconciles exactly; narrowing expansion to family/pathway/complex would reproduce Call 1's 22 but break the 27.",
      "resolution": "Kept the wider expansion and classified CEMIP as both_via_composite_label, since it was not named by a paper. A reviewer wanting Call 1's exact set should drop rows where lit_label_type is not in {family, pathway, complex, gene}."
    },
    "note": "27 is a gene-per-stratum count. Four genes are counted in two strata each (BIRC5, SOX10 and SPP1 in both NF1 MPNST and NF1 plexiform neurofibroma; EGFR in NF1 plexiform neurofibroma and NF2-SWN vestibular schwannoma), so 27 pairs collapse to 23 unique genes. Contract Call 1 enumerated 16 exact + 6 composite-only = 22 unique genes because it expanded only family/pathway/complex labels; expanding every label that carries constituent_genes (as phase3b_coverage.py does) adds CEMIP via the `other` label HYALURONAN, giving 23."
  },
